WEBVTT

00:01:00.206 --> 00:01:02.292
<i>Hell of an old satellite.</i>

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.712
<i>Gravity well caught it before
it could get into deep space.</i>

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.757
- <i>So it's</i> going <i>nowhere</i> fast.
- <i>Heinz, how's the satellite look?</i>

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.677
The recorder's the
only thing worth grabbing.

00:01:12.969 --> 00:01:14.262
Or do you want the whole sat?

00:01:14.887 --> 00:01:17.307
<i>No room in the hold. I'm gonna ice it.</i>

00:01:17.348 --> 00:01:19.225
Roger. Pulling out.

00:01:39.746 --> 00:01:45.877
Her Memories

00:01:58.973 --> 00:02:01.267
This is the Corona.
This is the Corona.

00:02:01.476 --> 00:02:03.436
Station 103, come in.

00:02:03.686 --> 00:02:06.564
<i>Station 103 here.
Go ahead, Corona.</i>

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:08.816
Final assignment completed.

00:02:08.941 --> 00:02:13.112
Obstacle drifting on route
PZ-302 has been destroyed.

00:02:13.905 --> 00:02:16.866
Now returning to Station 103.

00:02:16.991 --> 00:02:19.035
<i>Station 103, roger.</i>

00:02:20.078 --> 00:02:23.873
<i>Oh, I know your shift's over now, but
could you swing by route N on the way back?</i>

00:02:23.873 --> 00:02:26.834
Route N? That's not our area.

00:02:27.293 --> 00:02:31.255
<i>Some mining asteroids
have drifted loose over there.</i>

00:02:31.589 --> 00:02:36.094
<i>But the salvage ship covering
that area's had some trouble.</i>

00:02:36.302 --> 00:02:39.639
The Corona is the closest to them.

00:02:39.847 --> 00:02:42.183
<i>Come on, Ivanov. Just this once?</i>

00:02:42.642 --> 00:02:44.686
That's a no-can-do.

00:02:45.812 --> 00:02:48.731
We're tired.
Hell, the Corona's tired too.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.402
<i>Not even if I throw in overtime pay, Ivanov?</i>

00:02:52.735 --> 00:02:54.904
Sorry, you'll have to find someone else.

00:02:55.321 --> 00:02:59.033
<i>Oh well, then. Have a safe return.</i>

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.536
<i>I'll send you the
rendezvous point in a bit.</i>

00:03:01.703 --> 00:03:02.495
Rogen

00:03:03.913 --> 00:03:06.332
Goddamned management!

00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:09.919
Like we're a bunch of errand boys or something.

00:03:11.629 --> 00:03:13.965
Meanwhile, they only give us trash jobs!

00:03:15.133 --> 00:03:18.136
We are trash collectors,
so that sounds about right.

00:03:19.846 --> 00:03:20.930
You dumb shit!

00:03:21.139 --> 00:03:24.559
They used to say, "one man's
trash is another man's treasure!"

00:03:24.892 --> 00:03:29.230
Sure! Find just one wrecked ship,
and we could all buy California beach houses.

00:03:29.605 --> 00:03:33.985
That'd be nice, too bad there
aren't any more out there.

00:03:34.736 --> 00:03:35.862
Good work!

00:03:36.404 --> 00:03:40.241
Heinz, tell Aoshima about wrecks.

00:03:40.366 --> 00:03:41.117
Aoshima.

00:03:42.201 --> 00:03:45.872
If you want to see a wreck,
there's one right outside.

00:03:48.207 --> 00:03:49.876
Ah, sweet memories.

00:03:51.753 --> 00:03:54.338
I'll be back soon, Cecile.

00:03:54.589 --> 00:03:55.923
Be good a little longer, okay?

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:58.468
Oh, Cecile...!

00:03:58.468 --> 00:04:00.887
Hey, wait, there's Katherine
to think about too!

00:04:01.679 --> 00:04:05.475
What's a stud to do?
Do I even need to choose?

00:04:08.311 --> 00:04:10.438
There's the sound.
And out he slides!

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:17.320
That stuff comes with the job,
and being stuck out here.

00:04:17.528 --> 00:04:20.323
We just gotta put up
with it a bit longer.

00:04:20.656 --> 00:04:23.951
I just feel sorry for any woman
who falls for that jerk.

00:04:24.368 --> 00:04:25.411
Damn right.

00:04:25.953 --> 00:04:28.956
Hey, Heinz, you have a daughter, don't you?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.667
Though I think she's
only about ten, right?

00:04:33.961 --> 00:04:36.881
Oh, please.
I'm not into kids.

00:04:39.342 --> 00:04:40.760
We're all set.

00:04:46.766 --> 00:04:47.683
An SOS?

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:51.020
Aoshima, can you trace it?

00:04:55.817 --> 00:04:56.943
The hell?

00:05:15.294 --> 00:05:19.131
Hold it, Aoshima.
Is this some kind of joke?

00:05:19.715 --> 00:05:21.175
<i>Is that Madama Butterfly?</i>

00:05:21.676 --> 00:05:23.177
Is this really an SOS?

00:05:24.887 --> 00:05:27.557
It's coming from the
emergency channel, anyway.

00:05:28.057 --> 00:05:30.977
Man, we've worked our asses off today already.

00:05:31.018 --> 00:05:33.229
Now we gotta do a rescue op, unpaid?

00:05:33.646 --> 00:05:36.232
Can't we just call it in and go home?

00:05:36.315 --> 00:05:38.568
Idiot! Think that'll fly
with maritime law?

00:05:38.609 --> 00:05:40.987
If we don't go, they'll never
let us on a ship again.

00:05:41.696 --> 00:05:43.447
Aoshima, do you have the position?

00:05:43.531 --> 00:05:44.740
Hold on...

00:05:44.949 --> 00:05:48.244
Area RZ-30... 05?!

00:05:48.452 --> 00:05:50.621
See, I knew it!

00:05:51.455 --> 00:05:54.375
Well, ain't that great?
That's in Sargasso.

00:05:55.251 --> 00:05:57.295
The graveyard of space.

00:05:58.504 --> 00:06:00.798
So it's just calling out
for more old folks?

00:06:01.507 --> 00:06:04.635
The magnetic field in that
area can get pretty nasty.

00:06:06.804 --> 00:06:10.057
And this piece-of-shit
computer isn't mag-shielded!

00:06:10.266 --> 00:06:12.518
Won't that mean we're going in naked?

00:06:13.436 --> 00:06:15.229
When has that ever bothered you?

00:06:16.063 --> 00:06:18.608
H-Hey, I just don't want to be
a second SOS call, okay?

00:06:18.733 --> 00:06:19.775
Right, boss?

00:06:21.819 --> 00:06:22.987
Changing course!

00:06:56.812 --> 00:06:58.356
Jesus.

00:06:58.522 --> 00:07:01.150
We could build a
hundred beach houses!

00:07:01.359 --> 00:07:02.860
If we could haul it all back.

00:07:07.949 --> 00:07:10.117
Boss, the mag field's kicking up.

00:07:10.493 --> 00:07:12.328
And there's the computer done.

00:07:12.703 --> 00:07:14.538
All right, let's switch to the backup.

00:07:17.583 --> 00:07:21.837
I don't like where this is all headed.
How about you, Heinz?

00:07:23.714 --> 00:07:27.009
Aoshima, do you have an exact fix on the signal?

00:07:30.054 --> 00:07:31.347
Boss! Look at this!

00:07:33.307 --> 00:07:35.184
What the hell is that?

00:07:59.291 --> 00:08:01.961
It's huge!
Practically an asteroid!

00:08:02.712 --> 00:08:04.755
Looks like it's made up of the debris.

00:08:04.922 --> 00:08:06.298
Got a fix yet, Aoshima?

00:08:06.799 --> 00:08:09.677
<i>We're good. Getting some noise
now and then, though.</i>

00:08:13.472 --> 00:08:16.559
Could anyone actually
be living on this thing?

00:08:17.059 --> 00:08:18.602
Starting approach. Guide us in.

00:08:19.645 --> 00:08:22.481
<i>Wait! They're generating
centrifugal gravity, so-</i>

00:08:22.815 --> 00:08:24.316
Somebody must be home.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.778
Just pray they're not pirates.

00:08:45.296 --> 00:08:47.506
- Aoshima! There!
- Right!

00:08:57.725 --> 00:08:58.934
Is that an entrance?

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:01.729
<i>Hope they're not going to
start firing on us.</i>

00:09:02.188 --> 00:09:04.023
You'll just have to try knocking.

00:09:35.304 --> 00:09:38.182
All right, Heinz, we're going to
record proof of entry.

00:09:38.557 --> 00:09:39.642
Show me your ID.

00:09:46.232 --> 00:09:47.566
Okay, do it.

00:09:48.234 --> 00:09:52.071
<i>I, Heinz Beckner, and
my partner Miguel Costrella,</i>

00:09:52.404 --> 00:09:55.866
<i>acting on a mayday signal from
this vessel in area RZ-3005,</i>

00:09:56.075 --> 00:09:59.870
<i>are about to enter to
provide aid and rescue.</i>

00:10:00.079 --> 00:10:03.415
<i>October 12, 2092.</i>

00:10:07.711 --> 00:10:11.382
<i>October 12, 2092.</i>

00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:13.926
Okay, we're clear.

00:10:14.343 --> 00:10:15.594
All set over here.

00:10:33.112 --> 00:10:36.574
Damn, this equipment's ancient.

00:10:37.324 --> 00:10:40.244
That just means it's
easier for us to get in.

00:10:50.087 --> 00:10:50.921
Oxygen?

00:10:52.339 --> 00:10:55.926
Air seems fresh.
Radiation is in the green.

00:10:57.386 --> 00:10:58.470
How's the mag field?

00:10:58.804 --> 00:11:01.682
It's fine for now, but you
never know what will happen.

00:11:02.183 --> 00:11:03.434
Get back here in three hours.

00:11:03.767 --> 00:11:04.476
<i>Rfiger!</i>

00:11:04.643 --> 00:11:06.353
Easy for him to say, he's not here!

00:11:09.982 --> 00:11:11.942
Miguel, you okay?

00:11:16.155 --> 00:11:18.324
A hole straight into Hell, huh?

00:11:29.627 --> 00:11:30.794
The gravity's about to hit!

00:11:35.174 --> 00:11:36.508
I'm redding out!

00:11:36.842 --> 00:11:38.552
Should've taken more calcium.

00:11:41.931 --> 00:11:42.932
Miguel, move it!

00:11:50.814 --> 00:11:51.815
I can't gel UP!

00:11:52.775 --> 00:11:53.984
It's okay. Just pop it off!

00:12:04.203 --> 00:12:05.996
So, do we get the lady or the tiger?

00:12:06.538 --> 00:12:08.207
We'll find out once we're inside.

00:12:27.184 --> 00:12:28.394
What the hell?

00:12:29.186 --> 00:12:30.521
Incredible!

00:12:30.896 --> 00:12:32.564
Hey! Wait a sec!

00:12:40.155 --> 00:12:41.490
Are you seeing this, Pops?

00:12:41.865 --> 00:12:43.909
<i>Yeah. It's right out of a dream.</i>

00:12:45.327 --> 00:12:47.121
More like a nightmare!

00:12:55.713 --> 00:12:58.132
Hello? Anybody here?

00:13:09.018 --> 00:13:09.685
LGPS

00:13:24.658 --> 00:13:26.243
We should've seen someone by now.

00:13:26.452 --> 00:13:28.454
Aoshima, you still getting that SOS?

00:13:28.787 --> 00:13:30.247
<i>Yeah, definitely.</i>

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:33.542
For some reason it's weaker now, though.

00:13:34.293 --> 00:13:36.503
- The magnetic field?
- <i>I don't</i> think so.

00:13:37.921 --> 00:13:39.798
Miguel, look!

00:13:45.971 --> 00:13:47.639
What a babe!

00:13:47.931 --> 00:13:50.684
- The owner?
- I hope so.

00:13:51.643 --> 00:13:55.189
The brave Sir Miguel
comes to save Sleeping Beauty.

00:13:55.689 --> 00:13:57.024
I like the sound of that.

00:14:01.570 --> 00:14:02.279
What's wrong?

00:14:03.155 --> 00:14:04.406
- I saw...
- Hey, Miguel!

00:14:04.615 --> 00:14:06.075
A person! There's a woman!

00:14:06.241 --> 00:14:07.159
What?

00:14:39.817 --> 00:14:43.278
What are you doing?
Never seen a hologram before?

00:14:43.779 --> 00:14:46.365
So you really saw a woman?

00:14:46.657 --> 00:14:48.117
Yeah, well...

00:14:49.451 --> 00:14:51.703
She kind of up and vanished on me...

00:14:52.496 --> 00:14:55.207
Women always seem
to be ghosting you, huh?

00:14:55.416 --> 00:14:56.750
Shut up!

00:14:57.793 --> 00:14:59.545
Save the flirting for when we're back.

00:14:59.545 --> 00:15:00.879
Heinz, behind you!

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:07.678
<i>Madam, luncheon is now sewed.</i>

00:15:09.096 --> 00:15:12.891
<i>Madam, luncheon is now sewed.</i>

00:15:14.977 --> 00:15:15.727
What?

00:15:17.688 --> 00:15:18.772
What did it say?

00:15:27.573 --> 00:15:28.991
"Madam"?

00:15:33.328 --> 00:15:34.455
This looks great!

00:15:36.748 --> 00:15:38.167
Aoshima, can you see this?

00:15:38.459 --> 00:15:40.419
<i>Hey, Miguel! Are you nuts?</i>

00:15:40.711 --> 00:15:44.006
Hey now, just a perk
of the job. Right, Heinz?

00:15:45.382 --> 00:15:48.093
Who'd have thought we'd find
real wine way the hell out here?

00:15:49.219 --> 00:15:51.847
Though, I wonder why it's set for one?

00:15:52.973 --> 00:15:55.017
The madam lives by herself, apparently.

00:15:55.184 --> 00:15:55.976
Lucky me.

00:15:58.979 --> 00:16:00.731
Want some too, Heinz?

00:16:01.106 --> 00:16:02.232
You'll get sick.

00:16:06.487 --> 00:16:07.988
It's a nice vintage, though.

00:16:09.531 --> 00:16:10.949
With an excellent bouquet.

00:16:11.158 --> 00:16:14.036
<i>Come on, Miguel, cut it out!
You got a death wish?</i>

00:16:14.328 --> 00:16:15.913
You all need to lay off.

00:16:21.168 --> 00:16:23.212
Here's to you, madam!

00:16:29.635 --> 00:16:33.305
Serves you right.
You should be glad you're still alive.

00:16:34.306 --> 00:16:38.018
This! That! It's all garbage
made up to look pretty!

00:16:41.271 --> 00:16:44.858
Hey, Pops. Don't tell me
I have to knock on all of these?

00:16:45.192 --> 00:16:47.110
<i>Relax. Just keep going.</i>

00:16:49.238 --> 00:16:52.366
The SOS signal's about 70 meters ahead.

00:16:52.574 --> 00:16:53.575
<i>Okay-.</i>

00:16:53.909 --> 00:16:56.036
<i>I hope that isn't another fake too!</i>

00:17:03.794 --> 00:17:04.836
What's wrong, Heinz?

00:17:32.072 --> 00:17:34.116
Man, you broke it.

00:17:35.826 --> 00:17:37.703
It might've been valuable.

00:17:45.002 --> 00:17:48.380
Smells nice. This must be
the madam's dressing room.

00:17:51.133 --> 00:17:53.552
Damn, it just crumbled.

00:17:58.056 --> 00:17:59.474
Aoshima, you see this?

00:17:59.975 --> 00:18:02.227
<i>Yeah. Same lady from the portrait.</i>

00:18:10.235 --> 00:18:11.903
That jerk doesn't deserve her.

00:18:13.071 --> 00:18:15.824
Maybe she's an actress.
What do you think, Heinz?

00:18:20.495 --> 00:18:22.914
<i>A hologram? Of our madam?</i>

00:18:24.333 --> 00:18:26.501
Yeah. These trophies all belong to her.

00:18:27.419 --> 00:18:29.713
Or I should say,
the whole place looks to be.

00:18:29.921 --> 00:18:31.381
If she's still alive, anyway.

00:18:32.633 --> 00:18:37.763
"Eva Friedel, who sings evermore.
July 3, 2031."

00:18:39.139 --> 00:18:41.308
Aoshima, can you pull up some data on her?

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:46.980
<i>"Best Soloist, Italian Dance Festival."</i>

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:48.565
<i>"Grand Prize, Vienna Music Awards."</i>

00:18:49.066 --> 00:18:50.817
<i>"Gold Medal, Tokyo Opera Festival."</i>

00:18:51.109 --> 00:18:53.320
So our madam is an opera singer, huh?

00:18:55.155 --> 00:18:56.782
Living all alone...

00:18:57.908 --> 00:18:59.701
In a hall of past glories.

00:19:04.373 --> 00:19:07.417
No wonder she has so many dresses.

00:19:09.378 --> 00:19:11.755
All crumbling, now.

00:19:12.089 --> 00:19:14.091
<i>So wait, Why'd she send an SOS?</i>

00:19:14.716 --> 00:19:16.468
She was lonely, obviously!

00:19:16.551 --> 00:19:18.011
<i>What a damn pain.</i>

00:19:20.222 --> 00:19:22.516
Your Tosca today was excellent, Eva!

00:19:23.141 --> 00:19:24.726
Especially that duet.

00:19:24.935 --> 00:19:27.062
I can't think of anyone else for that role.

00:19:29.773 --> 00:19:30.524
Who's there?

00:19:35.362 --> 00:19:38.990
Naturally.
After all, I was singing with Carlo.

00:19:40.742 --> 00:19:41.368
Right?

00:19:55.716 --> 00:19:56.466
Madam...

00:19:58.009 --> 00:19:59.678
Did you see that, Aoshima?

00:19:59.845 --> 00:20:01.555
<i>Huh? See what?</i>

00:20:01.763 --> 00:20:05.350
Hey, cut the crap! She was just here.

00:20:10.772 --> 00:20:11.732
That's...

00:20:12.607 --> 00:20:14.109
...not a hologram!

00:20:17.571 --> 00:20:19.030
What's going on here?

00:20:19.531 --> 00:20:22.242
The flowers... I mean,
there was a woman here!

00:20:22.534 --> 00:20:23.869
It was the madam!

00:20:24.035 --> 00:20:25.203
Did you see her, Aoshima?

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.957
<i>I didn't see anything.
Maybe it was a ghost.</i>

00:20:28.957 --> 00:20:31.752
Goddammit, is everyone
trying to screw with me?

00:20:33.587 --> 00:20:37.215
"To my dearest Eva.
From your Carlo. June 15, 2005."

00:20:37.299 --> 00:20:41.803
"Eva"? Miguel, you're saying a
woman long dead was here?

00:20:42.596 --> 00:20:47.100
<i>We have to consider cold sleep, too.
Search the other rooms.</i>

00:20:47.142 --> 00:20:48.226
She was here!

00:20:48.351 --> 00:20:51.688
Sure. Ghosts don't
send out SOSes, do they?

00:20:52.022 --> 00:20:53.648
Stop patronizing me!

00:21:02.657 --> 00:21:05.202
We're running out of time,
Miguel. Let's split up.

00:21:07.245 --> 00:21:09.456
You're not scared of ghosts, are you?

00:21:10.415 --> 00:21:11.416
No way!

00:21:11.917 --> 00:21:15.003
Asshole. You think you're so cool.

00:21:47.202 --> 00:21:48.829
Aoshima, how's that SOS?

00:21:50.121 --> 00:21:51.498
<i>Let me check.</i>

00:21:54.167 --> 00:21:57.003
<i>Huh? It, uh... It's moving!</i>

00:21:57.379 --> 00:21:59.297
Moving? Then there must be a survivor!

00:21:59.798 --> 00:22:00.757
<i>Gotta be, right?</i>

00:22:03.176 --> 00:22:06.179
Great! Now the trip won't be a waste.

00:22:08.932 --> 00:22:09.599
Who's-?!

00:22:10.725 --> 00:22:11.726
Now that's freaky...

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:16.022
What kind of jerk makes a woman cry?

00:22:17.649 --> 00:22:19.276
It just keeps getting worse!

00:22:19.651 --> 00:22:22.904
A real cut-rate job.
Maybe they ran out of money?

00:22:25.699 --> 00:22:27.784
I don't think so.

00:22:28.326 --> 00:22:29.244
<i>Find something?</i>

00:22:29.744 --> 00:22:32.372
Our Madam Eva was born to nobility.

00:22:33.331 --> 00:22:34.749
<i>A princess, huh?</i>

00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:40.589
That explains the taste in decor.

00:22:41.006 --> 00:22:44.885
<i>She was born a prodigy, performing
as a soprano even as a kid.</i>

00:22:45.176 --> 00:22:47.554
<i>She was heralded as
"the diva of the century."</i>

00:22:49.139 --> 00:22:54.019
Then she met a star tenor,
Carlo Rambaldi, and they fell in love.

00:22:55.937 --> 00:22:59.733
Carlo is always by my side.
I couldn't be happier.

00:23:00.108 --> 00:23:02.986
So why's a woman like that
living in a place like this?

00:23:03.612 --> 00:23:05.822
Surrounded in the unreal.

00:23:05.989 --> 00:23:08.241
<i>Looks like things started going south.</i>

00:23:08.533 --> 00:23:10.660
<i>Something happened to her voice.</i>

00:23:12.746 --> 00:23:16.249
Yet she kept performing
on stage, for Carlo's sake.

00:23:19.169 --> 00:23:21.379
No one seems to know why she did that.

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:25.258
In fact, everyone started
lobbing criticism at her.

00:23:28.011 --> 00:23:30.138
Only I get to decide what I'm worth.

00:23:31.181 --> 00:23:35.060
<i>Basically, the world kept spinning,
but left her behind.</i>

00:23:35.143 --> 00:23:36.394
What about Carlo?

00:23:36.686 --> 00:23:39.356
<i>Guess what happened
right before their wedding.</i>

00:23:39.773 --> 00:23:41.566
- Did he die?
- Bingo!

00:23:41.775 --> 00:23:43.318
<i>Murdered, to be precise.</i>

00:23:43.568 --> 00:23:44.861
Wait, really? By whom?

00:23:45.528 --> 00:23:48.823
Lots of theories, like a crazy fan of Eva's.

00:23:49.074 --> 00:23:51.076
But they never arrested anyone for it.

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:54.120
After that, she disappeared
from public life.

00:23:54.537 --> 00:23:57.248
And came here to drown in her memories.

00:23:57.457 --> 00:23:59.334
A real tragedy.

00:24:03.588 --> 00:24:05.590
Sounds like my type of woman!

00:24:12.597 --> 00:24:13.390
What's wrong?

00:24:13.640 --> 00:24:15.308
The mag field's kicking up.

00:24:17.769 --> 00:24:19.396
Hey, you hear that? We're done.

00:24:20.397 --> 00:24:22.148
I'm pulling the plug on this rescue.

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:22.983
<i>Roger that.</i>

00:24:25.568 --> 00:24:28.738
Miguel! Do you copy?
Get back here!

00:24:30.281 --> 00:24:31.616
<i>I think I'm lost...</i>

00:24:32.492 --> 00:24:34.077
<i>All I'm seeing is scrap metal.</i>

00:24:38.456 --> 00:24:40.959
Would the madam really be down here?

00:24:49.300 --> 00:24:50.593
<i>What happened, Miguel?</i>

00:25:07.360 --> 00:25:08.528
<i>Is that the signal source?</i>

00:25:08.695 --> 00:25:09.904
How should I know?

00:25:20.498 --> 00:25:22.542
That melody... where have l...?

00:25:29.340 --> 00:25:30.175
It's the song!

00:25:30.508 --> 00:25:32.177
<i>Miguel, what's that sound?</i>

00:25:34.721 --> 00:25:37.974
Can you hear this?
It's the song! The SOS!

00:26:20.767 --> 00:26:22.519
I love you, Carlo!

00:26:24.896 --> 00:26:27.732
<i>Miguel! What's going on? Miguel!</i>

00:26:31.402 --> 00:26:33.279
Hey, Miguel!
What's going on?

00:26:33.863 --> 00:26:36.783
I just heard a woman's voice.
Hey, do you read me?

00:26:37.367 --> 00:26:38.743
Miguel!

00:27:09.399 --> 00:27:10.358
Who are you?

00:27:11.734 --> 00:27:13.945
Wait, you're...

00:27:31.129 --> 00:27:33.339
<i>You've gotten bigger, Emily.</i>

00:27:33.506 --> 00:27:36.509
<i>You're always saying that, Papa.</i>

00:27:38.511 --> 00:27:40.263
Can I open it here?

00:27:41.973 --> 00:27:43.808
What's inside?

00:27:46.352 --> 00:27:49.147
Wow! A space suit!

00:27:50.857 --> 00:27:52.901
I really wanted one!

00:27:53.902 --> 00:27:57.822
It's just like yours, Papa!
Now I can go into space with you, right?

00:27:58.031 --> 00:28:00.408
- Sure you can.
- Really?

00:28:00.909 --> 00:28:02.118
Thank you, Papa!

00:28:03.578 --> 00:28:04.579
Whoa, there.

00:28:07.832 --> 00:28:09.334
I love you so much, Papa!

00:28:14.255 --> 00:28:18.635
Oh, yeah. Papa,
the rocket's not working right!

00:28:18.885 --> 00:28:21.804
Good thing your papa's
really good with rockets.

00:28:25.058 --> 00:28:26.142
Mama, did you hear?

00:28:26.935 --> 00:28:28.853
Papa said he can take me up into space!

00:28:30.021 --> 00:28:33.066
Emily, we can talk after we eat.

00:28:33.274 --> 00:28:34.943
Aw...

00:28:38.071 --> 00:28:41.532
You love that suit, don't you?
But you'll get it dirty at the table.

00:28:41.824 --> 00:28:45.370
But he's going to take me into space!
Right, Papa?

00:28:48.039 --> 00:28:51.125
Emily, don't bother your father.

00:28:53.211 --> 00:28:57.715
It's just, I wanna be
with Papa all the time.

00:28:59.384 --> 00:29:01.344
I feel the same, Emily.

00:29:01.552 --> 00:29:05.014
We'd like him to be home
all the time. Right, dear?

00:29:11.896 --> 00:29:13.439
Mama, can I have the jam?

00:29:13.606 --> 00:29:16.276
Emily, you didn't eat your cucumbers again.

00:29:16.609 --> 00:29:17.902
Because I hate them!

00:29:18.111 --> 00:29:20.405
They don't let picky girls into space.

00:29:20.697 --> 00:29:22.031
That's not true!

00:29:26.995 --> 00:29:28.204
I meant it, before.

00:29:30.039 --> 00:29:31.541
I want you to stay here, always.

00:29:33.167 --> 00:29:35.128
My darling.

00:29:42.051 --> 00:29:44.304
<i>Heinz, do you read me? Come in!</i>

00:29:44.846 --> 00:29:45.513
<i>Heinz!</i>

00:29:46.597 --> 00:29:48.099
<i>Report! What's happening?</i>

00:29:48.558 --> 00:29:49.600
<i>What's going on?!</i>

00:29:53.313 --> 00:29:54.230
Emily...

00:29:54.689 --> 00:29:56.649
<i>Heinz, do you read me?</i>

00:29:57.817 --> 00:29:59.694
Yeah, I'm okay now.

00:29:59.861 --> 00:30:01.487
<i>What do you mean, now?</i>

00:30:01.696 --> 00:30:04.490
<i>We've been trying to
raise you for half an hour!</i>

00:30:06.159 --> 00:30:07.827
<i>What's going on over there?</i>

00:30:08.453 --> 00:30:10.038
<i>What's with those doll things?</i>

00:30:11.331 --> 00:30:12.665
I don't know...

00:30:14.667 --> 00:30:17.086
I have no idea,
but I'm going to bust them up!

00:30:24.177 --> 00:30:25.011
Shit!

00:30:25.678 --> 00:30:26.971
Is Miguel okay?

00:30:27.847 --> 00:30:29.724
I was hoping you could tell me.

00:30:30.641 --> 00:30:32.518
This mag field's a bitch!

00:30:32.894 --> 00:30:34.187
Just get out, now.

00:30:35.104 --> 00:30:36.606
My thoughts exactly!

00:30:39.942 --> 00:30:41.444
<i>The mag level's through the roof!</i>

00:30:45.031 --> 00:30:47.575
Did you two piss something off?

00:30:49.369 --> 00:30:50.870
Boss, this looks bad!

00:31:00.505 --> 00:31:02.006
<i>What's wrong, Eva?</i>

00:31:02.090 --> 00:31:04.300
<i>I'm afraid you're
going to leave me, Carlo.</i>

00:31:04.842 --> 00:31:05.885
Goddammit.

00:31:06.135 --> 00:31:08.888
What's Miguel saying?
He's been acting weird.

00:31:09.305 --> 00:31:11.349
Do you have eyes on Eva? Heinz!

00:31:13.518 --> 00:31:14.560
Just some angels!

00:31:14.852 --> 00:31:17.355
<i>I'll always be with you, Eva.</i>

00:31:17.522 --> 00:31:18.272
<i>Truly?</i>

00:31:21.067 --> 00:31:24.278
Yes. We'll be together... forever.

00:31:24.821 --> 00:31:27.031
Shit. There he goes,
after another woman.

00:31:28.366 --> 00:31:29.158
<i>I'm so happy, Carlo.</i>

00:31:29.158 --> 00:31:29.742
I'm so happy, Carlo.

00:31:30.535 --> 00:31:33.704
Eva, my life is yours alone.

00:31:40.336 --> 00:31:41.212
I love you!

00:31:42.046 --> 00:31:43.756
Thank you, Carlo.

00:31:44.173 --> 00:31:46.843
Now I'm not sure which one to rescue.

00:31:50.972 --> 00:31:51.764
Miguel!

00:31:55.476 --> 00:31:56.602
Where are you, Miguel?

00:32:03.943 --> 00:32:04.610
Miguel...

00:32:07.697 --> 00:32:09.115
Come to me, Eva.

00:32:09.365 --> 00:32:12.702
As long as these roses bloom, we-

00:32:12.952 --> 00:32:15.246
Shit, he's completely fallen for it.

00:32:17.623 --> 00:32:19.625
Miguel, come back! Miguel!

00:32:23.087 --> 00:32:24.547
_ <i>W -'Miguel!
hat s happening?</i>

00:32:25.089 --> 00:32:28.676
Heinz, come in!
Heinz, do you read?

00:32:29.427 --> 00:32:31.304
Boss, look!

00:32:37.477 --> 00:32:39.479
Christ, it's eating the pod.

00:32:40.313 --> 00:32:43.107
The thing's a regular gourmet. Shit!

00:32:47.236 --> 00:32:48.905
What the hell is it now?

00:32:49.030 --> 00:32:49.906
It's the debris!

00:32:50.364 --> 00:32:54.452
And not just that, the Corona
is being dragged in too!

00:32:54.660 --> 00:32:56.245
Son of a...

00:32:56.454 --> 00:32:57.038
Heinz, do you read?

00:32:57.038 --> 00:32:58.539
<i>Heinz, do you read?</i>

00:33:04.003 --> 00:33:04.754
Miguel!

00:33:08.925 --> 00:33:10.343
Miguel! Don't go!

00:33:16.098 --> 00:33:18.351
Son of a bitch!

00:33:23.481 --> 00:33:25.858
Miguel, this isn't real!

00:33:31.531 --> 00:33:33.282
Don't you get it, Miguel?

00:33:33.658 --> 00:33:35.618
This is all just her memories!

00:33:48.631 --> 00:33:49.382
Miguel!

00:33:51.592 --> 00:33:52.468
Miguel!

00:33:59.225 --> 00:34:00.601
<i>Why do you interfere?</i>

00:34:12.863 --> 00:34:15.241
Carlo lives forever.

00:34:15.741 --> 00:34:18.369
With me, in my memories.

00:34:18.703 --> 00:34:19.370
What?

00:34:20.037 --> 00:34:22.039
You should know
exactly what I mean.

00:34:24.208 --> 00:34:27.795
Why pretend?
Why turn away from reality?

00:34:29.463 --> 00:34:30.756
Carlo is dead!

00:34:38.889 --> 00:34:40.641
I've made him eternal.

00:34:41.183 --> 00:34:41.976
My Carlo.

00:34:43.352 --> 00:34:44.228
You what?

00:34:44.645 --> 00:34:48.441
Within my memories,
his heart will never change.

00:34:50.526 --> 00:34:51.527
It was you...

00:34:52.612 --> 00:34:53.529
You killed him!

00:34:57.825 --> 00:35:00.536
How can you say that
reality even compares?

00:35:02.079 --> 00:35:03.748
Have you forgotten?

00:35:04.624 --> 00:35:05.791
Allow me to remind you!

00:35:27.772 --> 00:35:28.522
The rocket...

00:35:29.690 --> 00:35:31.317
Papa!Look!

00:35:32.693 --> 00:35:34.695
Now I can go into space with you!

00:35:35.196 --> 00:35:36.197
No, Emily!

00:35:36.530 --> 00:35:37.281
Papa?

00:35:41.494 --> 00:35:42.620
Don't do it!

00:35:45.164 --> 00:35:46.582
Papa!

00:36:40.261 --> 00:36:42.221
Welcome back, Papa!

00:36:44.890 --> 00:36:47.893
Did you bring me a present?

00:36:48.227 --> 00:36:48.894
Did you?

00:36:49.353 --> 00:36:51.772
I've been a good girl, waiting so long!

00:36:54.275 --> 00:36:55.693
Emily!

00:36:58.070 --> 00:36:59.029
Oh, God...

00:37:00.281 --> 00:37:01.490
You're alive.

00:37:03.033 --> 00:37:04.910
Papa, you're squishing me.

00:37:07.079 --> 00:37:08.497
Sorry, Emily.

00:37:10.624 --> 00:37:13.127
Welcome home, darling.

00:37:16.881 --> 00:37:18.048
Come on, Papa!

00:37:18.716 --> 00:37:19.216
Wait...

00:37:19.925 --> 00:37:22.011
Come on, let's go inside.

00:37:22.470 --> 00:37:23.554
Come on! Come on!

00:37:24.221 --> 00:37:25.556
Okay, calm down now.

00:37:27.641 --> 00:37:29.685
Let's stay here forever, Papa!

00:38:05.262 --> 00:38:06.180
Emily!

00:38:09.642 --> 00:38:10.684
Emily!

00:38:12.019 --> 00:38:12.853
Emily.

00:38:15.356 --> 00:38:16.190
Emily!

00:38:20.611 --> 00:38:21.612
Emily!

00:38:25.157 --> 00:38:27.409
Emily's right here.

00:38:28.494 --> 00:38:29.411
Emily.

00:38:34.041 --> 00:38:35.084
Emily...

00:38:45.719 --> 00:38:47.096
Emily!

00:38:53.853 --> 00:38:54.812
You can't just...

00:38:56.105 --> 00:38:56.939
Memories aren't...

00:38:58.232 --> 00:38:59.650
You can't hide in the past!

00:39:23.465 --> 00:39:25.926
Aoshima, can we fire the analyzer cannon?

00:39:27.219 --> 00:39:29.221
Yeah, it's ready when you are!

00:39:29.722 --> 00:39:32.057
Wait, though!
They're still inside!

00:39:32.892 --> 00:39:34.810
If we don't, we'll all be dead!

00:39:35.185 --> 00:39:37.688
Aoshima! Aim at the central air lock!

00:39:38.022 --> 00:39:39.732
Put the coordinates on-screen!

00:40:01.295 --> 00:40:02.630
The computer...

00:40:04.340 --> 00:40:05.341
It's gone mad!

00:40:34.328 --> 00:40:36.622
Welcome home, darling.

00:40:44.004 --> 00:40:47.633
Damn it! We're gonna die and
still be buried in garbage!

00:40:51.845 --> 00:40:53.430
It's what you always wanted!

00:40:53.764 --> 00:40:55.057
Now just hang on...

00:40:59.478 --> 00:41:01.689
Heinz, forgive me!

00:41:41.729 --> 00:41:42.771
More of her victims!

00:42:40.329 --> 00:42:43.707
- Good morning, Eva.
- Good morning, Carlo.

00:42:43.999 --> 00:42:45.876
So beautiful today.

00:42:47.544 --> 00:42:49.671
You mean the roses?

00:42:50.089 --> 00:42:52.091
Of course I mean you, Eva.

00:42:53.550 --> 00:42:55.094
Though they do look splendid.

00:42:57.721 --> 00:43:01.350
This is the peak of their season.

00:43:02.810 --> 00:43:06.522
Whenever I see a rose,
I'm reminded of you.

00:43:06.980 --> 00:43:09.483
Oh? So there's times you forget me?

00:43:11.360 --> 00:43:14.530
Yet here I am, thinking of you always...
